# devdoc/DOC-INDEX.tsv is DERIVED, and it is merged by UNION.
#
# The manifest carries one row per file under devdoc/, and its rows are a SET:
# line order carries no meaning (the file already holds rows appended out of
# sequence, and the writer splices a new row at the whole-corpus sort position
# without moving any existing line). Two branches that each add a document
# therefore never disagree ABOUT the file — they each hold one line the other has
# not seen — but git's default three-way merge calls that a content conflict
# (measured 2026-10-19 on a fixture clone: `CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in
# devdoc/DOC-INDEX.tsv`). The same fixture with this attribute merged with ZERO
# conflicted paths and BOTH rows present.
#
# THE ATTRIBUTE IS SPELLED FOR ONE PATH, NOT A PATTERN. Union concatenates
# conflicting hunks, which is correct exactly where the file is a set of
# INDEPENDENT lines and catastrophic where two edits touch one function — so
# nothing else in this tree may inherit it.
#
# A UNION MERGE IS CONFLICT-FREE, NOT CONVERGED: the result can carry a
# duplicated path, and a resolution that kept one side silently parts with the
# other's line. `gopi tool doccheck` prints how far behind the tree is
# (`N row(s) behind`, with the per-shape breakdown) and the writer converges it
# in one idempotent command (`python3 tools/docclass/classify.py <repo>`) — see
# internal/docindex/docindex_behind.go and devdoc/derived-manifest-merge.md.
devdoc/DOC-INDEX.tsv merge=union
